    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green.\n\n## What I did\n\nAdded a duplicate-telephone check to the `POST /api/owners` pipeline as small, self-contained units rather than modifying existing functions:\n\n1. **`RequireUniqueOwnerTelephone`** (new function) \u2014 runs after `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`, so it compares the 10-digit normalized form. Scans existing owners via `OwnerRepository.findAll()` and throws a checked `DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException` on a match.\n2. **`DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException`** (new checked exception) \u2014 so it can be thrown and escalated.\n3. **`DuplicateOwnerTelephoneExceptionHandler`** (new handler) \u2014 responds `409 CONFLICT` with a `ProblemDetail` body, matching the existing escalation style.\n4. **`...DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException.yml`** (new escalation wiring).\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted a single `unique:` step between `normalize` and `build`, sharing the write transaction.\n\n### Structural impact\nThe only existing file *changed* is `owners.POST.yml` (3 added lines, no methods edited). Everything else is new small classes with one method and near-zero surrounding complexity, so no existing function's cost was incurred \u2014 the whole change follows the AGENTS.md one-function-per-step convention.\n\nBoth new tests (`coreRejectsDuplicateTelephone`, `functionalityAllowsDistinctTelephone`) and the full suite pass.",
